---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import portrait from "../assets/icon.png";
import ContactIcons from "../components/ContactIcons.astro";
import MeCode from "../components/MeCode.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import TypedName from "../components/TypedName.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

---

<Layout>
	<div class="flex flex-col gap-10 lg:flex-row lg:items-center lg:justify-between">
		<header class="flex items-center gap-6">
			<Image
				alt="Pieter's profile"
				src={portrait}
				width="240"
				class="h-24 w-24 shrink-0 rounded-full border-2 border-edge object-cover object-[50%_18%] sm:h-28 sm:w-28"
			/>
			<div>
				<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-fg">
					<TypedName text="Pieter Willekens" />
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-2 text-fg-muted"><span class="text-comment select-none">// </span>Dad, developer and drummer.</p>
				<div class="mt-4">
					<ContactIcons />
				</div>
			</div>
		</header>
		<div class="lg:w-105 lg:shrink-0">
			<MeCode />
		</div>
	</div>

	<Section title="at work" command=":e work.md">
		<p>
			I'm tech lead on the <a href="https://www.patientjourneyapp.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Patient Journey App</a> at{" "}
			<a href="https://www.interactivestudios.nl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Interactive Studios</a>, an app that guides patients through their
			treatment by giving them the right information at exactly the right moment. My work runs the whole stack:
			application architecture, code review, CI/CD, and keeping our Kubernetes clusters happy. I've been writing code
			since I was 14, and part of Interactive Studios since 2012.
		</p>
	</Section>

	<Section title="technologies" command=":e stack.md">
		<p>
			Laravel on the backend, React and TypeScript on the frontend, React Native + Expo on mobile, and Kubernetes
			underneath it all. Lately I've been poking at <a href="https://www.rust-lang.org" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Rust</a>, mostly for fun and
			sometimes for speed. Open source is close to my heart, as an idea and in practice: I contribute where I can and
			want to do more of it. See <a href="/projects/">projects</a> for the results.
		</p>
	</Section>

	<Section title="homelab" command=":e homelab.md">
		<p>
			The most over-engineered corner of the house: a dedicated Proxmox box that runs Home Assistant, an Unraid server
			hosting Immich, Paperless-ngx, Syncthing, and more containers than strictly necessary (protected by a parity
			disk, whatever RAID level that makes it), and a UniFi network tying it all together.
		</p>
		<p>
			The 3D printers count as lab equipment too: a Bambu Lab P1S and a heavily modded Ender 3 running Klipper and
			Mainsail. Tinkering with it all is half the point; the other half is that the lights turn on by themselves.
		</p>
	</Section>

	<Section title="outside of work" command=":e life.md">
		<p>
			When I'm not at a keyboard, I'm with my partner, our two kids, and the dog. The rest of my time goes to drumming,
			collecting vinyl, 3D printing, gaming, and evenings with friends.
		</p>
		<p>
			The drumming happens on an acoustic kit when the house allows it and an e-kit when it doesn't, to a soundtrack of
			Drum 'n Bass, deadmau5, rock, metal, metalcore, and much more.
		</p>
		<p>
			Big sci-fi and fantasy fan, on screen and on paper: Star Wars, Lord of the Rings, and Brandon Sanderson's
			Mistborn series.
		</p>
		<p>Also: astronomy and physics. I will happily lose an evening to a video about black holes.</p>
	</Section>
</Layout>

<style>
	p + p {
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}
</style>
